    "body": "@zcorpan, are you excited about researching and spec'ing this?\n\nOne question we'll be forced to confront is how tolerant to be of browsers other than Chrome, Firefox and Safari adding stuff to the UA string. Opera and Edge do this, and my default browser on Debian does too: `Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64; rv:38.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/38.0 Iceweasel/38.2.0`. Presumably you can find this for WebKit too, on the same form as the Chrome UA string or possibly with the extra appended.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/144745529/reactions",
