    "created_at": "2015-10-02T09:46:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-10-02T11:22:30Z",
    "body": "OK, so for each of _Chrome_, _Gecko_ and _WebKit_, I think we will have these variants:\n- Other browsers using the same engine, or pretending to, like Opera and Edge.\n- Mobile versions of the same browser, with the string \"Mobile\" in a specific place.\n- The UI widget version of the browser, e.g. [Android WebView](https://developer.chrome.com/multidevice/user-agent) with \"Version/4.0\" and [iOS UIWebView](http://stackoverflow.com/questions/2143763/does-uiwebview-send-the-same-user-agent-in-the-request-headers-as-mobile-safari) exluding \"Safari\".\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
